title: 'Session capstone — the Academy: cold no-op → live, self-correcting, web-foraging learning loop'
summary: 'One marathon session took the Paradigm Classroom from an unbootstrapped no-op to a working, demonstrable learning system, end-to-end on real data. Opened with 3 verified framework fixes (double-tilde aspect unreachability, the f:N essence-hash collision, the /api/warpline security cluster) surfaced by a self-study convene; then designed the whole Academy (vision spec, 7 Pencil screens, a 6-flow HTML prototype, the Expeditions external-knowledge model with ratified trust decisions TD-2026-06-25-044); then BUILT it: bootstrapped the gate, wrote /forage + upgraded /class (Step-0 Orientation + THE STAND), ported a read-only Academy section into the Suite, ran the first live gated term (Rune''s learning refined + a peer cert, scoreboard honestly null), closed the two-loops gap (gatedPromoteJournalEntry stamps peer vs the quarantined legacy gate), and made Expeditions real (journal provenance envelope + Arky''s genuine web dive → 3 cited external candidates on the board, the barrel-file challenger refuted against our 9 tsup-bundled barrels).'
